  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1012 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nThe main talking point in the long term period will be a drastic \nchange in temperatures after the rainfall clears out Thursday \nmorning and upper level ridging/sfc high pressure moves into the \narea from the west. Highs on Thanksgiving are forecast to be \ncapped in the upper 50s at this time as cloud cover lingers \nthroughout the prime diurnal heating hours of the afternoon. These\nclouds should gradually clear from west to east during the \nevening to overnight hours and low temperatures will drop to near \nor below freezing for all of the Tennessee Valley Friday morning. \nThese temperatures are forecast to be around 10 degrees below \nnormal. Friday and Friday night bring another relatively cool day \nwith highs peaking in the 50s once again before overnight lows \ndrop into the upper 20s to lower 30s. This pattern will be short-\nlived as the sfc high slowly shifts closer to the Tennessee Valley\nand a warming trend takes over through the weekend. Highs on \nSaturday and Sunday are forecast to reach the 60s under mostly \nclear skies with overnight lows remaining in the 30s Saturday \nnight. Overall, should allow pleasant conditions for any \nadditional travel plans through the holiday weekend. However, be \nsure to bundle up in multiple layers if outdoors overnight.",
